WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:06.470
The DCEU gets deeper, both literally and figuratively,
with the release of Aquaman, a two-hour-plus

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:11.670
plunge into the murky abyss that is undersea
politics, reluctant beefcake princes, and

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.700
wet and wild superpowers.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.880
What's left to take away, now that the Atlantean
prince's journey of self-discovery and his

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.600
rise to power is over?

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:25.000
According to Aquaman lore, Atlantis fell into
the ocean because Atlan, the king of Atlantis,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.110
got too greedy with his power.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:32.471
He places his powerful Trident into an unknown
device, an explosion happens, and all of Atlantis

00:00:32.471 --> 00:00:33.471
gets wrecked.

00:00:33.471 --> 00:00:38.350
But what, exactly, could possibly cause a
catastrophe that would destroy an entire,

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.840
ultra-advanced civilization?

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.970
We never find out.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.760
Sure, it's probably all just magical mumbo
jumbo, but as the most powerful ruler on the

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.920
planet, what promises were made to tempt Atlan
towards even greater power?

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.870
While you don't really need to explain the
mechanics of mystical powers in a fantasy

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.160
world, we're talking about the world's biggest
magical accident here.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.400
Exploding the known world warrants a little
more explanation.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:06.120
Some of the tridents possessed by Atlanteans
have certain powers, although we see early

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.020
on that trident magic is poorly defined.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:14.470
Sometimes, Atlanteans can even do all kinds
of magic without swinging around pointy weapons.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:18.170
Aquaman can communicate with fish, and Mera
can control the flow of water, and both are

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.720
skills that aren't common to all Atlanteans.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.500
So, the rules of wet magic are pretty loose.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.330
So, what exactly can Atlan's Trident do?

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:31.049
"In this Trident resides the power of Atlantis."

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.741
We know that his trident is a legendary symbol
of unity for all of the people of the Seven

00:01:35.741 --> 00:01:39.170
Kingdoms, and that it somehow caused the fall
of Atlantis.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:44.280
But aside from granting Arthur Curry the power
of spontaneously golden, scaly pecs, its powers

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.680
are undefined.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.350
Maybe the Trident amplifies Aquaman's power
over marine life...though he didn't really

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.990
seem to have all that much trouble with chatting
up crabs before.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.700
Has the power been inside Arthur Curry all
along?

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:58.270
Did his heart grow three sizes that day?

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.120
We just don't know yet.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:05.960
Much of DC's cinematic world depends on the
fact that humans just aren't that observant.

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:10.459
Themyscira is hidden in the middle of the
ocean by a magical veil that only a few people

00:02:10.459 --> 00:02:14.439
have managed to see through, and Atlantis
is well-hidden because about 80% of the Earth's

00:02:14.439 --> 00:02:15.790
oceans remain unexplored.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.870
But even within Atlantis is yet another hidden
world that nobody seems to know about: the

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:24.819
unnamed, dinosaur-filled world of the Earth's
core.

00:02:24.819 --> 00:02:29.659
Readers of DC comics know that there's a canonical
inner Earth called Skartaris that appears

00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:34.879
in DC Comics' Warlord series, and that land
is accessed via a hole in the North Pole.

00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:39.469
That sword-and-sorcery world of Skartaris
bears a striking resemblance to this inner-Earth.

00:02:39.469 --> 00:02:44.870
But going even deeper into comic lore, within
Skartaris is a city called Shamballah: an

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.000
ancient Atlantean city, not unlike where Atlan's
corpse is found.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.800
Warlord's small collection of dedicated fans
need to know: did we just get Skartaris on

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.240
the big screen?

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:00.400
Perhaps one of Aquaman's biggest unanswered
questions is…pretty much everything about

00:03:00.419 --> 00:03:01.650
Black Manta.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:06.409
David Kane seems to be a technological supergenius
to rival the likes of Tony Stark.

00:03:06.409 --> 00:03:10.329
He can steal experimental stealth submarines
from the government, but he'd rather just

00:03:10.329 --> 00:03:13.949
be a pirate instead of doing something financially
fulfilling with his genius.

00:03:13.949 --> 00:03:18.620
He's also in communication with Orm, though
we're never told just exactly how Manta and

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:23.059
Orm made their love connection, despite Orm's
distrust of surface dwellers.

00:03:23.059 --> 00:03:25.120
Maybe they met on the Love Boat?

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.760
Manta's one and only goal is to kill Aquaman,
which aligns with Orm's aims perfectly.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.989
Manta not only gets a squad of fish-men to
command, but his very own experimental Atlantean

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:35.989
tech.

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:40.390
While this underwater tech is the only way
to really take down Aquaman, Manta wandering

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:43.709
around with this stuff on the surface seems
like a loose end that Orm would never want

00:03:43.709 --> 00:03:46.939
to leave dangling… and that's exactly what
happens.

00:03:46.939 --> 00:03:51.720
If there was some kind of failsafe against
humans using Atlantean tech against Atlantis,

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.520
we never find out what it was.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:59.669
Atlantis, Xebel, The Trench, The Desert, the
Fisherman, and the Brine Kingdom make up most

00:03:59.669 --> 00:04:03.409
of the tribes of Atlantis… but what's the
seventh kingdom?

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:08.329
Early posters for Justice League featuring
Aquaman bore the slogan 'Unite the Seven',

00:04:08.329 --> 00:04:12.400
but once Justice League actually came out,
there were only six heroes.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.820
Aquaman revealed only six of the seven kingdoms
that broke off from ancient Atlantis by name,

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.400
so there's a missing kingdom somewhere.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.220
It's possible that this missing kingdom is
the Earth's core, also known as the Hidden

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.220
Sea.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:31.509
But it's also possible that perhaps the missing
kingdom is, in fact, the surface world, given

00:04:31.509 --> 00:04:36.470
that Aquaman is destined to 'Unite the Seven,'
and both he and Atlan's Trident are powerful

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:37.870
symbols of this unity.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:40.669
"You could unite our worlds one day."

00:04:40.669 --> 00:04:44.550
It's also possible that DC is saving a seventh
kingdom for a sequel.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.220
Bizarro World, anyone?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.360
"Not even close."

